Build an unofficial Windows installer from a tag

Purpose: a Windows installer of the overlay at one fixed public URL,
marked in its About dialog, that nobody can mistake for an official
Rnote release.

Approach: upstream's release-windows.yml also runs on the
overlay-build tag (git overlay-build), so toolchain and action updates
arrive with every rebase. Overlay steps only add a version mark
(+overlay-<sha> via the 'version-extra' meson option) and upload the
installer to one prerelease on that tag, titled and described as
unofficial with a link to upstream's releases.

Constraints: on a fork the release and dispatch paths of
release-windows.yml and dist.yml never run, so no general-release
installer or source archive is built there. Upstream behaviour is
unchanged. 'just configure' interpolates unquoted, so version-extra
stays free of spaces and parentheses.
